    "answerText": "If you configure and assign a Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to the user, Teams checks the userΓÇÖs outgoing calls against the Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to determine whether their dialed number matches a number-pattern that you've defined in the online voice-routing policy.\n\nIf you configure and assign a Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to the user, Teams checks the userΓÇÖs outgoing calls against the Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to determine whether their dialed number matches a number-pattern that you've defined in the online voice-routing policy.\n\n[Microsoft documentation context ΓÇö conceptual_explanation]\nPlanning Teams dial plans for Teams Phone ΓÇ║ Dial plans and routing considerations ΓÇ║ Direct Routing online voice-routing policy with Calling Plan\nDocument: Planning Teams dial plans for Teams Phone Heading Path: Planning Teams dial plans for Teams Phone -> Dial plans and routing considerations -> Direct Routing online voice-routing policy with Calling Plan If a user has a Calling Plan license, that userΓÇÖs outgoing calls are automatically routed through the Microsoft Calling Plan PSTN infrastructure. If you configure and assign a Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to the user, Teams checks the userΓÇÖs outgoing calls against the Direct Routing online voice-routing policy to determine whether their dialed number matches a number-pattern that you've defined in the online voice-routing policy. If thereΓÇÖs a match, the call is routed through the Direct Routing route. If thereΓÇÖs no match, the call is routed through the Calling Plan PSTN infrastructure. For more information, see Direct Routing voice routing policy considerations.\nSource: Planning Teams dial plans for Teams Phone\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/dial-plans-routing-overview\n\nOnly supported portions should be answered.\n\nMissing authoritative domain coverage: teams_powershell\n\nNot established from available authoritative evidence (mandatory:entity:csv-export:output-transformation): The Teams-side data retrieval for this workflow is authoritatively covered where supported; CSV export is a generic PowerShell step not currently covered by Relay's authoritative corpus.\n\nNot established from available authoritative evidence (missing_authority): The Teams-side data retrieval for this workflow is authoritatively covered where supported; CSV export is a generic PowerShell step not currently covered by Relay's authoritative corpus.\n\nPlanning Teams dial plans for Teams Phone ΓÇö https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/dial-plans-routing-overview",
